  "title": "Proxy — Meta-layer theoretical reference for regime-bound measurement",
  "description": "Curated meta-layer reference for the Proxy meta-principle: measurement of complex systems is cartography, not verdict. Any observable substituted for an unobserved quantity is regime-bound, with validity defined by the alignment of regime, proxy, placement, episenter, and compression. Synthesises the EFC source paper with the wider methodological literature on surrogate endpoints (Prentice, Fleming-DeMets), biomarker validation (FDA-NIH BEST), mirror systems (Rizzolatti, Gallese), and entropy proxies (Casali PCI, Lempel-Ziv). Includes P1-P4 sealed predictions and bridges to HomoFluxus, Autopoiesis, cognitive, and medicine layers.",
